  "Each paragraph of original-en comes from exactly one source; no paragraph mixes translations.",
  "Original-en keeps the translators' own gap marks, brackets, '(?)' and asterisks. Footnote glosses printed by Jastrow-Clay that resolve a pronoun ('i. e., Enkidu', 'the man', 'He was thrown and therefore vanquished') are inlined in parentheses only where marked '(i. e., ...)' or '( ... )' in the text; all other footnotes and scholarly commentary are omitted.",
